Brahmā hails Viśvāmitra as R̥ṣi and departs to heaven --- Viśvāmitra resumes great austerities --- Mēnakā bathes at Puṣkara and captivates Viśvāmitra --- Viśvāmitra keeps Mēnakā ten years in his hermitage --- Ashamed Viśvāmitra blames gods for stealing his tapas --- Viśvāmitra dismisses trembling Mēnakā and performs fierce Kauśikī tapas --- Frightened gods prompt Brahmā to grant Maharṣi rank but withhold Brahmarṣi word --- Viśvāmitra undertakes wind-eating five-fire tapas as Indra summons Rambhā